 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "what",
   "h2": "What an adverb does",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "lead": "An adjective describes a noun. An <b>adverb</b> describes a verb: it says how, when or how long something is done. \"He works <b>happily</b>\"; \"they arrived <b>at last</b>\"."
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "servus <u class=\"c\">laete</u> <u class=\"v\">laborat</u>.",
      "en": "The slave <b>works happily</b>.",
      "note": "<em>laete</em> comes from <em>laetus</em>, happy."
     }
    },
    {
     "facts": [
      "To make an adverb from a 2-1-2 adjective, take the stem and add <em>-e</em>: <em>laetus</em>, <em>laete</em>.",
      "Take the stem from the feminine: <em>misera</em> gives <em>misere</em>, and <em>pulchra</em> gives <em>pulchre</em>.",
      "An adverb never changes its ending."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "forms",
   "h2": "Making adverbs",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "table": {
      "head": [
       "Adjective",
       "Adverb",
       "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
       [
        "<em>laetus</em>, happy",
        "laet<b>e</b>",
        "happily"
       ],
       [
        "<em>iratus</em>, angry",
        "irat<b>e</b>",
        "angrily"
       ],
       [
        "<em>stultus</em>, foolish",
        "stult<b>e</b>",
        "foolishly, stupidly"
       ],
       [
        "<em>miser, misera</em>, wretched",
        "miser<b>e</b>",
        "wretchedly, miserably"
       ],
       [
        "<em>pulcher, pulchra</em>, beautiful",
        "pulchr<b>e</b>",
        "beautifully"
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "note": "Other words end in <em>-e</em> too, such as the infinitive <em>monere</em>. When the word is built on an adjective you know, it is an adverb."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
